<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13420"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 3:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think how it goes to prove insanity they would have to show that the defendent is unable to appreciate the nature and quality of the wrongfulness of his acts, he is mentally retarded or suffers from a mental disease that would include paranoid schizophrenea and or auditory illusions. <BR>I don&#39;t think they could prove Dennis Rader insane in the classic sense so they would have to show that he is mentally defective. He suffers from a mental disease that drives him to commit crimes and leave him mentally disabled, mentally incapable or mentally impaired while commiting his crimes. <BR>I think they will try to show that he is mentally incapacitated where he is rendered temporarily and substantially incapable of either appraising the nature of his conduct and the quality of the wrongfulness of his acts or resisting doing it as the result of the influence of an alter-ego that drives him to commit the crimes and then disappears leaving him to return to normal life and then returns intermitenly. This is where his self-diagnosed Factor X comes into play. His planning, carrying out and taunting are done while an alternative personality has taken controll of him. <BR>Maybe Pheonix can help me out on this.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13420-->
<!--Post: 13422--><!--Time: 1115245525-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13422"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 3:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just read the Crim. Law 2 Insanity thread that I didn&#39;t see before so I will post any further questions I may have on this topic of insanity defense over there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13422-->
